{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[G]Some glad morning [G]when this life is o'er,
[C]I'll fly [G]away
[G]To a home on [G]God's celestial shore,
[D7]I'll fly [G]away
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[G]I'll fly away, [G7]O glory,
[C]I'll fly [G]away (in the morning)
[G]When I die, [G]hallelujah,
[G]by and by [D7]I'll fly [G]away
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
When the shadows of this life have grown,
I'll fly away
Like a bird from prison bars has flown,
I'll fly away
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
Just a few more weary days, and then,
I'll fly away
To a land where joys shall never end,
I'll fly away
{end_of_chorus}
